 "description": "Live US macro data with the derived signals, not just the raw levels: Fed funds rate, 2Y and 10Y Treasury yields plus the 2s10s YIELD CURVE SPREAD (with its direction \u2014 steepening or flattening \u2014 and an inverted flag), CPI inflation year-over-year, the broad trade-weighted dollar index (a different index from the ICE dollar index, so read its direction rather than comparing its level), VIX and M2 money supply. Every series carries its previous reading, so direction is available without a second call. The curve slope, not the level of any single yield, is the liquidity and cycle signal: inversion has preceded every US recession, and re-steepening out of an inversion usually marks the start of easing \u2014 the moment that matters for risk assets. VIX explains crypto drawdowns that have no crypto-native cause.",
